wq 0.8.0

Commands
========
  wq                       repl
  wq <script path>         script exec
  wq exec [<code>|-]       inline exec
  wq fmt <script>          format

Options
=======
1. Generic
  -h, --help               show this help
  -v, -V, --version        show wq version

2. Runtime
  -p, --print              print final evaluation result
  -d, --debug [<f/a>]      config debug flags, def=inst
  -i, --interpreter <name> select interpreter
  -b, --builtins <preset>  select builtins preset
  -w, --wqdb               use wqdb
  --no-bt                  disable backtrace

  debug flags         token ast inst wqdb-1 wqdb-2
  debug aliases       0=off 1=inst 2=inst,ast 3=inst,ast,token
                      4=inst,ast,token,wqdb-1,wqdb-2
  interpreters        [d]efault, [p]rofiler, [s]ample
  builtins            [a]ll, [c]onstrained, [p]ure, [m]inimal

3. fmt
    --nlcd            Newline after closing delimiters
    --nbc             No bracket calls
    --olw             One line wizard

Examples
========
1. Run a script:
  wq /path/to/script.wq
2. Run code & dump instructions & print final evaluation:
  wq exec "echo(1+1)" -d1 -p
3. Ditto + dump AST + profiler
  wq exec "echo(1+1)" -i p -d2 -p
